+// The LIGHT-UNIT convention, which is a different question from "is the scene-referred pipeline
+// running" and has to be answered by a different authority (SceneReferredSpec.md D4,
+// decisions/s2-engine-side-switch.md).
+//
+// The sun colour these callers are correcting was computed inside CTimeOfDay::UpdateEnvLighting
+// under E3DPARAM_SCENE_REFERRED, and it is cached there until the next time-of-day update. Asking
+// the post-effect bus instead would be asking a different clock: the bus value changes the frame
+// ccam publishes it, the sun's value changes only when the time of day is re-evaluated. Reading
+// the same global that produced the number keeps the correction and the number in lockstep, which
+// is the entire point of the manual undos this gates.
+bool CRendererResources::IsSceneReferredLightUnits()
+{
+	if (!gEnv->p3DEngine)
+		return false;
+
+	Vec3 v(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
+	gEnv->p3DEngine->GetGlobalParameter(E3DPARAM_SCENE_REFERRED, v);
+	return v.x > 0.5f;
+}
